        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f97b606a667e4b2388cdec13be4d2209",
      "statement": "Deep Agents is a three-layer stack: LangGraph is the runtime (state, checkpoints, streaming, interrupts), LangChain's create_agent is the agent abstraction (model + tools + middleware forming the agent loop), and Deep Agents is an opinionated harness on top of create_agent that does not introduce a new runtime.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L12-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:591b743f68a1f0d4a3711e21813aa4b1e01123fccc91f89bd8eb5d94bab5187e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ba9b336bb60e42d49c621fdf907bb775",
      "statement": "Local package dependencies within the monorepo are editable, so changes in one package are visible to sibling packages that depend on it during development.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/DEVELOPMENT.md#L49-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7695993b3d943d06b2de7b895b0152f7c3ffd6bb6b71db8d824b463ff08905d2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c37640b23c16470c84a12c100352974b",
      "statement": "The recommended entry paths differ by task: dcode (libs/code) is the fastest way to try Deep Agents as a terminal coding agent, while the deepagents SDK (libs/deepagents) is the route for building a custom agent.",
